{"id":"mahabharata-2-038","work":"mahabharata","part":2,"partName":"सभापर्व","partNameEn":"Sabha Parva","unit":38,"title":"अष्टात्रिंशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 38 · Shishupala abuses Bhishma and Krishna","summary":{"en":"Shishupala heaps scorn on Bhishma as a disgrace to his line, mocks his vow and his carrying off of Amba, and derides Krishna's boyhood deeds, killing a bird, a horse and a bull, as no great feats. He compares Bhishma to a lying old swan.","kn":"ಶಿಶುಪಾಲನು ಭೀಷ್ಮನನ್ನು ವಂಶಕ್ಕೆ ಕಳಂಕವೆಂದು ತಿರಸ್ಕರಿಸಿ, ಅವನ ವ್ರತವನ್ನೂ ಅಂಬೆಯ ಅಪಹರಣವನ್ನೂ ಹಂಗಿಸಿ, ಪಕ್ಷಿ, ಕುದುರೆ, ಗೂಳಿಯನ್ನು ಕೊಂದ ಶ್ರೀಕೃಷ್ಣನ ಬಾಲ್ಯದ ಕೃತ್ಯಗಳು ದೊಡ್ಡ ಸಾಹಸಗಳಲ್ಲವೆಂದು ಅಪಹಾಸ್ಯ ಮಾಡುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಭೀಷ್ಮನನ್ನು ಸುಳ್ಳು ಹೇಳುವ ಮುದಿ ಹಂಸಕ್ಕೆ ಹೋಲಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"शिशुपाल भीष्म को कुल का कलंक कहकर तिरस्कार करता है, उनके व्रत और अम्बा के हरण का उपहास करता है, और श्रीकृष्ण के बचपन के कार्यों, एक पक्षी, घोड़े और बैल को मारने, को कोई बड़ी बात न मानकर हँसी उड़ाता है। वह भीष्म की तुलना एक झूठे बूढ़े हंस से करता है।","te":"శిశుపాలుడు భీష్ముని వంశానికి కళంకమని తిరస్కరించి, అతని వ్రతాన్ని, అంబాపహరణాన్ని ఎగతాళి చేసి, పక్షిని, గుర్రాన్ని, ఎద్దును చంపిన శ్రీకృష్ణుని బాల్యకృత్యాలు గొప్ప సాహసాలు కావని హేళన చేస్తాడు. భీష్ముని అబద్ధాలాడే ముసలి హంసతో పోలుస్తాడు.","ta":"ஶிஶுபாலன் பீஷ்மரைக் குலத்துக்கு இழுக்கு என்று இகழ்ந்து, அவர் விரதத்தையும் அம்பையைக் கவர்ந்ததையும் ஏளனம் செய்து, பறவை, குதிரை, காளையைக் கொன்ற ஸ்ரீகிருஷ்ணரின் சிறுவயதுச் செயல்கள் பெரிய சாதனைகள் அல்ல என்று கேலி செய்கிறான். பீஷ்மரைப் பொய் சொல்லும் முதிய அன்னத்துக்கு ஒப்பிடுகிறான்.","ml":"ശിശുപാലൻ ഭീഷ്മരെ തന്റെ വംശത്തിന് അപമാനമെന്ന് പരിഹസിക്കുന്നു; അദ്ദേഹത്തിന്റെ പ്രതിജ്ഞയെയും അംബയെ കവർന്നതിനെയും പരിഹസിക്കുന്നു; കൃഷ്ണന്റെ ബാല്യകാല പ്രവൃത്തികളെ, ഒരു പക്ഷിയെയും കുതിരയെയും കാളയെയും കൊന്നതിനെ, വലിയ വീരകർമമല്ലെന്ന് പറഞ്ഞ് ആക്ഷേപിക്കുന്നു. ഭീഷ്മരെ നുണ പറയുന്ന വൃദ്ധ അരയന്നത്തോട് അദ്ദേഹം ഉപമിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 2.38; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Apr 19 2006","sections":[{"title":"शिशुपालवधपर्व","titleEn":"Shishupalavadha Parva (Slaying of Shishupala)","verses":[{"text":"शिशुपाल उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Shishupala said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"विभीषिकाभिर्बह्वीभिर्भीषयन्सर्वपार्थिवान् ।\nन व्यपत्रपसे कस्माद्वृद्धः सन्कुलपांसनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Frightening all the kings with many threats, why are you not ashamed, old man, disgrace of your family?"}},{"n":2,"text":"युक्तमेतत्तृतीयायां प्रकृतौ वर्तता त्वया ।\nवक्तुं धर्मादपेतार्थं त्वं हि सर्वकुरूत्तमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It suits you, living in the third nature, to speak words devoid of dharma; for you are the foremost of all the Kurus."}},{"n":3,"text":"नावि नौरिव संबद्धा यथान्धो वान्धमन्वियात् ।\nतथाभूता हि कौरव्या भीष्म येषां त्वमग्रणीः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Like boats tied to a boat, or a blind man following a blind man, such are the Kauravas, Bhishma, whose leader you are."}},{"n":4,"text":"पूतनाघातपूर्वाणि कर्माण्यस्य विशेषतः ।\nत्वया कीर्तयतास्माकं भूयः प्रच्यावितं मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By recounting his deeds, beginning with the killing of Putana, you have unsettled our minds all the more."}},{"n":5,"text":"अवलिप्तस्य मूर्खस्य केशवं स्तोतुमिच्छतः ।\nकथं भीष्म न ते जिह्वा शतधेयं विदीर्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma, proud fool who wish to praise Keshava, why does your tongue not split into a hundred pieces?"}},{"n":6,"text":"यत्र कुत्सा प्रयोक्तव्या भीष्म बालतरैर्नरैः ।\nतमिमं ज्ञानवृद्धः सन्गोपं संस्तोतुमिच्छसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma, he is one whom even mere boys should revile; you, an elder in knowledge, wish to praise this cowherd."}},{"n":7,"text":"यद्यनेन हता बाल्ये शकुनिश्चित्रमत्र किम् ।\nतौ वाश्ववृषभौ भीष्म यौ न युद्धविशारदौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"If he killed a bird in his childhood, what is wonderful in that, Bhishma? And the two, a horse and a bull, were unskilled in fighting."}},{"n":8,"text":"चेतनारहितं काष्ठं यद्यनेन निपातितम् ।\nपादेन शकटं भीष्म तत्र किं कृतमद्भुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If he knocked over a lifeless piece of wood, a cart, with his foot, Bhishma, what marvel was done there?"}},{"n":9,"text":"वल्मीकमात्रः सप्ताहं यद्यनेन धृतोऽचलः ।\nतदा गोवर्धनो भीष्म न तच्चित्रं मतं मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"If he held up a mountain, no bigger than an anthill, for seven days, Bhishma, then Govardhana was in my view no wonder."}},{"n":10,"text":"भुक्तमेतेन बह्वन्नं क्रीडता नगमूर्धनि ।\nइति ते भीष्म शृण्वानाः परं विस्मयमागताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma, he ate a lot of food while playing on a mountain top; hearing that, you were greatly amazed."}},{"n":11,"text":"यस्य चानेन धर्मज्ञ भुक्तमन्नं बलीयसः ।\nस चानेन हतः कंस इत्येतन्न महाद्भुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And that mighty Kamsa, on whose food he had eaten, knower of dharma, was killed by him; that is no great marvel."}},{"n":12,"text":"न ते श्रुतमिदं भीष्म नूनं कथयतां सताम् ।\nयद्वक्ष्ये त्वामधर्मज्ञ वाक्यं कुरुकुलाधम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma, you have surely not heard what good people say: what I shall tell you, you who ignore dharma, vilest of the Kurus."}},{"n":13,"text":"स्त्रीषु गोषु न शस्त्राणि पातयेद्ब्राह्मणेषु च ।\nयस्य चान्नानि भुञ्जीत यश्च स्याच्छरणागतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Good people always teach that one should not raise weapons against women, cows, brahmins, one whose food one has eaten, or one who has sought refuge."}},{"n":14,"text":"इति सन्तोऽनुशासन्ति सज्जना धर्मिणः सदा ।\nभीष्म लोके हि तत्सर्वं वितथं त्वयि दृश्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"So the righteous, who are good, ever instruct; Bhishma, all of that proves false in you in this world."}},{"n":15,"text":"ज्ञानवृद्धं च वृद्धं च भूयांसं केशवं मम ।\nअजानत इवाख्यासि संस्तुवन्कुरुसत्तम ।\nगोघ्नः स्त्रीघ्नश्च सन्भीष्म कथं संस्तवमर्हति ॥","meaning":{"en":"You speak as if you do not know that Keshava is, to me, an elder and greater in knowledge; praising him, best of the Kurus, how can a killer of a cow and of a woman deserve praise?"}},{"n":16,"text":"असौ मतिमतां श्रेष्ठो य एष जगतः प्रभुः ।\nसंभावयति यद्येवं त्वद्वाक्याच्च जनार्दनः ।\nएवमेतत्सर्वमिति सर्वं तद्वितथं ध्रुवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If, because of your words, Janardana, this best of the wise and lord of the world, thinks: All this is so, then all of it is surely false."}},{"n":17,"text":"न गाथा गाथिनं शास्ति बहु चेदपि गायति ।\nप्रकृतिं यान्ति भूतानि भूलिङ्गशकुनिर्यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"A song does not instruct the singer, however much he sings; beings return to their own nature, like the bhulinga bird."}},{"n":18,"text":"नूनं प्रकृतिरेषा ते जघन्या नात्र संशयः ।\nअतः पापीयसी चैषां पाण्डवानामपीष्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surely this base nature is yours, no doubt; and so a worse one is thought to belong to these Pandavas as well,"}},{"n":19,"text":"येषामर्च्यतमः कृष्णस्त्वं च येषां प्रदर्शकः ।\nधर्मवाक्त्वमधर्मज्ञः सतां मार्गादवप्लुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"for whom Krishna is the most worthy of honour and you are the guide: you, a talker of dharma who ignores dharma, fallen from the path of the good."}},{"n":20,"text":"को हि धर्मिणमात्मानं जानञ्ज्ञानवतां वरः ।\nकुर्याद्यथा त्वया भीष्म कृतं धर्ममवेक्षता ॥","meaning":{"en":"What man, best of the knowing, who knew himself to be righteous, would act as you have done, Bhishma, while looking to dharma?"}},{"n":21,"text":"अन्यकामा हि धर्मज्ञ कन्यका प्राज्ञमानिना ।\nअम्बा नामेति भद्रं ते कथं सापहृता त्वया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma, you who think yourself wise, how was the maiden named Amba, who wanted another man, abducted by you, knower of dharma? May you be well."}},{"n":22,"text":"यां त्वयापहृतां भीष्म कन्यां नैषितवान्नृपः ।\nभ्राता विचित्रवीर्यस्ते सतां वृत्तमनुष्ठितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The girl you abducted, Bhishma, the king, your brother Vichitravirya, who followed the conduct of the good, did not want."}},{"n":23,"text":"दारयोर्यस्य चान्येन मिषतः प्राज्ञमानिनः ।\nतव जातान्यपत्यानि सज्जनाचरिते पथि ॥","meaning":{"en":"While you, thinking yourself wise, looked on, children were born to his two wives by another man, along a path the good would follow."}},{"n":24,"text":"न हि धर्मोऽस्ति ते भीष्म ब्रह्मचर्यमिदं वृथा ।\nयद्धारयसि मोहाद्वा क्लीबत्वाद्वा न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma, you have no dharma; this celibacy is in vain, which you keep out of delusion or impotence; there is no doubt."}},{"n":25,"text":"न त्वहं तव धर्मज्ञ पश्याम्युपचयं क्वचित् ।\nन हि ते सेविता वृद्धा य एवं धर्ममब्रुवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knower of dharma, I never see any gain for you; you have not served the elders who spoke dharma thus."}},{"n":26,"text":"इष्टं दत्तमधीतं च यज्ञाश्च बहुदक्षिणाः ।\nसर्वमेतदपत्यस्य कलां नार्हति षोडशीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sacrifice, giving, study and sacrifices with abundant fees: all this is not worth a sixteenth part of having a child."}},{"n":27,"text":"व्रतोपवासैर्बहुभिः कृतं भवति भीष्म यत् ।\nसर्वं तदनपत्यस्य मोघं भवति निश्चयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever is done with many vows and fasts, Bhishma, all that is surely fruitless for the childless."}},{"n":28,"text":"सोऽनपत्यश्च वृद्धश्च मिथ्याधर्मानुशासनात् ।\nहंसवत्त्वमपीदानीं ज्ञातिभ्यः प्राप्नुया वधम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, childless and old, teaching false dharma, you too will now meet death at the hands of your relatives, like the swan."}},{"n":29,"text":"एवं हि कथयन्त्यन्ये नरा ज्ञानविदः पुरा ।\nभीष्म यत्तदहं सम्यग्वक्ष्यामि तव शृण्वतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Other men, knowers of old, tell this tale; I shall tell it rightly, Bhishma, as you listen."}},{"n":30,"text":"वृद्धः किल समुद्रान्ते कश्चिद्धंसोऽभवत्पुरा ।\nधर्मवागन्यथावृत्तः पक्षिणः सोऽनुशास्ति ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Long ago, they say, there was an old swan by the shore of the ocean who spoke of dharma but acted otherwise, and he instructed the birds."}},{"n":31,"text":"धर्मं चरत माधर्ममिति तस्य वचः किल ।\nपक्षिणः शुश्रुवुर्भीष्म सततं धर्मवादिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Do dharma, not adharma, was his teaching; the birds, Bhishma, always listened to the dharma-speaker."}},{"n":32,"text":"अथास्य भक्ष्यमाजह्रुः समुद्रजलचारिणः ।\nअण्डजा भीष्म तस्यान्ये धर्मार्थमिति शुश्रुम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, we hear, other egg-born creatures of the sea waters brought him food, for the sake of dharma, Bhishma."}},{"n":33,"text":"तस्य चैव समभ्याशे निक्षिप्याण्डानि सर्वशः ।\nसमुद्राम्भस्यमोदन्त चरन्तो भीष्म पक्षिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Placing all their eggs near him, the birds roamed and enjoyed themselves in the sea water."}},{"n":34,"text":"तेषामण्डानि सर्वेषां भक्षयामास पापकृत् ।\nस हंसः संप्रमत्तानामप्रमत्तः स्वकर्मणि ॥","meaning":{"en":"That sinful swan ate the eggs of all of them as they were careless, while he stayed alert to his own business."}},{"n":35,"text":"ततः प्रक्षीयमाणेषु तेष्वण्डेष्वण्डजोऽपरः ।\nअशङ्कत महाप्राज्ञस्तं कदाचिद्ददर्श ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, as the eggs were dwindling, another bird, very wise, grew suspicious and once saw him."}},{"n":36,"text":"ततः स कथयामास दृष्ट्वा हंसस्य किल्बिषम् ।\nतेषां परमदुःखार्तः स पक्षी सर्वपक्षिणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the swan's wrong, that bird, afflicted by great sorrow for them, told all the birds."}},{"n":37,"text":"ततः प्रत्यक्षतो दृष्ट्वा पक्षिणस्ते समागताः ।\nनिजघ्नुस्तं तदा हंसं मिथ्यावृत्तं कुरूद्वह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, having seen it with their own eyes, the birds gathered, O Kuru, and killed that swan of false conduct."}},{"n":38,"text":"ते त्वां हंससधर्माणमपीमे वसुधाधिपाः ।\nनिहन्युर्भीष्म संक्रुद्धाः पक्षिणस्तमिवाण्डजम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So these kings too, enraged, Bhishma, may kill you, who share the swan's nature, as the birds did that egg-bird."}},{"n":39,"text":"गाथामप्यत्र गायन्ति ये पुराणविदो जनाः ।\nभीष्म यां तां च ते सम्यक्कथयिष्यामि भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"People who know the old lore also sing a verse about this; I shall tell it to you properly, Bhishma."}},{"n":40,"text":"अन्तरात्मनि विनिहिते\nरौषि पत्ररथ वितथम् ।\nअण्डभक्षणमशुचि ते\nकर्म वाचमतिशयते ॥","meaning":{"en":"With your inner self concealed, you cry falsehood, winged one; your eating of eggs is impure, and your deed outweighs your words."}}]}]}